From: PonWrt
Subject: [PATCH] luci-base: raise the request field limit to 10 MB

LuCI rejects a form whose fields hold more than 100 kB each. OpenClash's
config file page carries the whole config twice in text areas, so with a
config over 100 kB every Apply on that page fails with "the value exceeds
the maximum allow size". 10 MB fits large subscription configs and is
still small next to the memory of the routers this targets.
---
--- a/modules/luci-base/ucode/http.uc
+++ b/modules/luci-base/ucode/http.uc
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 import { run_plugins } from 'luciplugins';
 
 // luci.http module scope
-export let HTTP_MAX_CONTENT = 1024*100;		// 100 kB maximum content size
+export let HTTP_MAX_CONTENT = 1024*1024*10;	// 10 MB maximum content size
 
 // Decode a mime encoded http message body with multipart/form-data
 // Content-Type. Stores all extracted data associated with its parameter name
